EQUIVALENT: publisher: a subdomain is a different publisher
    unreachable, and the reason is worth knowing: the `www.` strip is redundant given what follows it. `_registrable_domain` takes the last two labels (three under a known multi-label suffix), and `www.northwind-stats.example` has the same last two labels as `northwind-stats.example`. Removing the strip therefore cannot change any domain this function returns. It stays because it makes the intent legible at the point of use, and because the label arithmetic below it is one edit away from needing it.
